From 360c49c19f1373d0e94ef45d09ae8f1378fb7458 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 11:15:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] bcm2835-i2cd: I2C bus 1 of the Raspberry Pi as a scheme

/scheme/i2c/1/scan lists the addresses that answer; /scheme/i2c/1/<addr>
reads and writes the device's registers at the file offset. GPIO 2 and 3
go to ALT0 through bcm2835-gpiod, SCL is 100 kHz from the firmware's core
clock. Polled BSC1, no interrupts.

Refs #39

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
